  "body": {
    "id": "thm:bounded-local-allocation-frontier-corollary",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Let fixed finite endpoints \\(L<U\\) have width \\(W=U-L\\), and let \\(q_n\\to q^\\star\\).  Uniformly whenever \\(\\zeta_n=n^{1/6}(q_n-q^\\star)\\) ranges over a compact subset of the simplex tangent plane,\n\\[\n\\rho_{n,[L,U]}^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q_n)\n=\\frac{W^2}{n}+W^2n^{-4/3}\\{\\mathsf P(\\zeta_n)-C_3\\}\n+o(n^{-4/3}).\n\\]\nThus the bounded iid array retains the unrestricted bounded sharp correction if and only if\n\\(n^{1/6}(q_n-q^\\star)\\to0\\).  If \\(q_n\\to q^\\star\\) and\n\\(n^{1/6}\\|q_n-q^\\star\\|\\to\\infty\\), then\n\\[\nn^{4/3}\\left\\{\\rho_{n,[L,U]}^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q_n)-W^2/n\\right\\}\\longrightarrow\\infty.\n\\]\nThe allocation threshold is unchanged and its risk penalty is multiplied by \\(W^2\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "L",
      "U",
      "W",
      "q_n",
      "q^\\star",
      "\\zeta_n",
      "n",
      "\\rho_{n,[L,U]}^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q)",
      "\\mathsf P(\\zeta)",
      "C_3"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:local-allocation-frontier",
      "thm:bounded-outcome-endpoint-transfer",
      "thm:bounded-sharp-face-corner-corollary"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "For every \\(n\\), endpoint transfer gives\n\\[\n\\rho_{n,[L,U]}^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q_n)\n=W^2\\rho_n^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q_n).\n\\tag{35}\n\\]\nMultiply the uniform expansion from \\(\\textnormal{thm:local-allocation-frontier}\\) by the fixed constant \\(W^2\\).  Its remainder remains \\(o(n^{-4/3})\\), uniformly on the same compact subsets, proving the displayed bounded expansion.  Because \\(W^2>0\\), equation (35) preserves the necessary-and-sufficient condition for matching the unrestricted sharp correction.  Finally,\n\\[\nn^{4/3}\\left\\{\\rho_{n,[L,U]}^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q_n)-W^2/n\\right\\}\n=W^2n^{4/3}\\left\\{\\rho_n^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q_n)-1/n\\right\\},\n\\]\nso the binary divergence conclusion implies the bounded one.",
